migration_guide_summary:
- Callers using for-await-of: keep using response.stream() (unchanged) but adopt AbortSignal-based cancellation: const controller = new AbortController(); for await (const chunk of response.stream({signal: controller.signal})) { ... }
- Browser apps: switch to response.webStream() to get native backpressure and pipeTo/transform streams. Use streamToAsyncIterable if you have async-iterator libraries you can't change.
- To support both: use response.dualStream({prefer: 'web'|'async'}) which returns a wrapper exposing both as methods. This wrapper manages a single underlying source and serializes close/cancel operations.
